r target-match enforcement.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"Workflow resolve-dispatch step (lines 44-49): if no DISPATCH-NOTE.md found in PR diff → enforce=false → exit 0. The workflow paths: filter triggers on branch-protection-log.md changes, so the check-invocation-log-entry job runs but exits 0. The check-invocation-log-entry.sh script is never invoked. A PR containing only branch-protection-log.md changes passes enforcement silently.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"Operator (or compromised committer) can add a fabricated invocation log entry for a target repo that was never actually onboarded. The entry satisfies the Threshold A log-completeness check. The audit trail becomes untrustworthy for forensic reconstruction of which repos were actually protected.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"In the resolve-dispatch step, if no DISPATCH-NOTE is found but the PR modifies branch-protection-log.md, fail closed (exit 1) rather than exit 0. Alternatively: when enforce=false and branch-protection-log.md is in the diff, emit a warning and exit 0 only if STATUS.md also changed (indicating a non-cascade infrastructure update). Document the exception explicitly in the workflow comment.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SAFE-MIN-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MIN\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"The posture-degradation guard for required_status_checks counts contexts from the raw before-JSON (.required_status_checks.contexts // [] | length). A before-JSON with contexts: [\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"] (one empty-string element) has length=1, bypassing the --i-understand-restore-removes-required-checks ack requirement, even though an empty-string context name is semantically equivalent to no effective check.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"enable-required-check.sh:650-654: restore_contexts from RESTORE_TARGET_JSON via jq length; if restore_contexts -eq 0 then exit 2 without ack. An empty-string element ([\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"]) has length 1 so the guard does not fire. Schema validation (lines 344-357) only checks required_status_checks is (dict|Non