{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/r1-completeness_governance.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":619541,\"duration_api_ms\":618355,\"num_turns\":45,\"result\":\"I now have sufficient data to produce the review. Let me compile the findings.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"review_id\\\": \\\"r1-completeness_governance\\\",\\n  \\\"slice\\\": \\\"WP-SCP-024-024B-extras\\\",\\n  \\\"lens\\\": \\\"completeness_governance\\\",\\n  \\\"reviewer\\\": \\\"Sonnet\\\",\\n  \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-05-10\\\",\\n  \\\"summary\\\": \\\"024B-extras delivers all scope items called out in the DISPATCH-NOTE: --restore mode with GET→PUT transform + posture-degradation guards, forward-mode safety check (path-pinned workflow lookup, no branch filter), ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass 3-gate playbook, CI workflow wiring with tooling-slice job-body short-circuit, D-047 filed, STATUS.md chain entry, VERSIONING.md all four new flags added, and the step-7 PLACEHOLDER with TF-024B-STEP7-DEMO-001 correctly open and merge-blocking. All R8 carry-forward items (CORR-001/002/003, SAFE-001/002, Bootstrap) are addressed. The step-7 AC is correctly left unchecked. One MAJ gap: TF-024B-core-WORKFLOW-MITIGATION-001 was slated to close in this slice but STATUS.md still shows future tense under the wrong section; the chain entry omits a closure note despite the workflow case-statement delivering the goal. One MIN: D-047 is absent from STATUS.md 'Recent decisions'. Two nits: DISPATCH-NOTE 'paths-ignore' terminology vs. actual 'paths:' trigger; ADOPT-001 §12.8 chains the SLO to invariant 7 by reference rather than inlining it.\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CG-MAJ-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"TF-024B-core-WORKFLOW-MITIGATION-001 not