US.md 'Recent decisions'; opportunistically add D-044 as well (omitted from 024B-core chain but listed in the same section pattern).\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CG-nit-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"nit\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"DISPATCH-NOTE describes the CI workflow trigger as using 'paths-ignore' syntax; the actual implementation uses a 'paths:' include-list plus job-body short-circuit.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"DISPATCH-NOTE scope table reads 'paths-ignore: [docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[AB]*/**,...]'. Actual workflow uses 'paths: [docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[C-Z]*/**,...]' with tooling-slice short-circuit in the job-body case statement. The functional effect is equivalent but the YAML key is different.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Future slice authors using this DISPATCH-NOTE as a template may implement a literal paths-ignore, unintentionally widening the trigger surface beyond cohort-cascade PRs.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Update the DISPATCH-NOTE CI workflow paragraph to say 'paths: 024[C-Z]*/**' and clarify that tooling-slice bypass is via job-body case statement rather than a paths-ignore key.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CG-nit-002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"nit\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"ADOPT-001 §12.8 does not state the <30 min rollback SLO inline; it chains to it via 'WP-SCP-024 invariant 7' in the Reference line only.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"§12.8 body covers Gate 1/2/3, WARNING/CAUTION callouts, and Reference pointers but contains no inline SLO statement. The Reference line cites 'WP-SCP-024 invariant 7' which carries the '<30 min from operator decision to merge-restored state' SLO text.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Adopter operators following §12.8 during an incident must chase a plan-doc reference to find the SLO target; low severity since reference chain is intact but adds friction at incident time.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add a one-line SLO note to §12.8 body: 'Target: <30 min from operator decision to merge-restored state (invariant 7); confirmed by step-7 real-repo round-trip demo before 024C opens.'\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"ac_map\\\": {\\n    \\\"--restore mode logic correct\\\": \\\"PASS — script lines 600–716: GET→PUT transform via validate_restore_source_json, APPLY_FAIL=0 wrap, posture-degradation flags checked, required_signatures POST/DELETE sub-resource, pre-restore GET before PUT.\\\",\\n    \\\"Forward-mode safety check path-pinned + no branch filter\\\": \\\"PASS — check_forward_mode_safety() queries by workflow_id (path=policy-check-wrapper.yml) without &branch= filter; guarded under RESTORE_MODE -eq 0.\\\",\\n    \\\"--expected-wrapper-sha validates against git tags\\\": \\\"PASS — validate_expected_wrapper_sha_against_tags resolves SHA via gh api repos/.../git/ref/tags/<tag>; mutex with --i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci enforced.\\\",\\n    \\\"ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass 3-gate\\\": \\\"PASS — §12.8 between §12.7.15 and §13; Gate 1/2/3 with concrete commands; WARNING + CAUTION callouts; REQUIRED --expected-wrapper-sha at Gate 3.\\\",\\n    \\\"CI workflow with paths-ignore + SHA-pinned actions\\\": \\\"PASS — .github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml; paths: 024[C-Z]*/**; checkout@de0fac2e... (SHA-pinned); tooling-slice case short-circuit.\\\",\\n    \\\"Tests cover all --restore mode behaviours\\\": \\\"PASS — test file lines 1729–2938: make_restore_fake_gh, run_restore_case, GET→PUT transform assertion, APPLY_FAIL, posture-degradation, DELETE/POST 404 suppression, absolute path, --expected-wrapper-sha tag validation, mutex tests.\\\",\\n    \\\"D-047 filed\\\": \\\"PASS — DECISIONS.md D-047 row present; Last Updated 2026-05-10.\\\",\\n    \\\"Operator-interactive step-7 demo evidence\\\": \\\"OPEN (merge-blocking) — restore-roundtrip-evidence-PLACEHOLDER.md present; TF-024B-STEP7-DEMO-001 (open) in STATUS.md.\\\",\\n    \\\"R8-CORR-001 closed in 024B-core\\\": \\\"PASS — not applicable to extras.\\\",\\n    \\\"R8-CORR-002 restore-mode guard scoping\\\": \\\"PASS — prior_restore_evidence_present called only inside check_forward_mode_safety() which is gated on RESTORE_MODE -eq 0.\\\",\\n    \\\"R8-CORR-003 closed in 024B-core\\\": \\\"PASS — not applicable to extras.\\\",\\n    \\\"R8-SAFE-001 --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification WARNING + CAUTION\\\": \\\"PASS — §12.8 WARNING + CAUTION callouts present; log block CAUTION emitted (script line 515); D-047 acknowledges escape hatch.\\\",\\n    \\\"R8-SAFE-002 uncommitted Gate-1 working-tree diff check\\\": \\\"PASS — prior_restore_evidence_present() checks git diff HEAD branch-protection-log.md (lines 413–438).\\\",\\n    \\\"R8 Bootstrap defect\\\": \\\"PASS — paths: 024[C-Z]*/** excludes 024[AB]*; job-body case exits 0 for 024B-extras; STATUS.md and branch-protection-log.md in paths: so tooling-slice PR still triggers + exits 0.\\\",\\n    \\\"VERSIONING.md four new flags\\\": \\\"PASS — --expected-wrapper-sha, --i-understand-restore-removes-admin-enforcement, --i-understand-restore-removes-required-checks, --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification all present in §Branch-protection helper.\\\",\\n    \\\"Plan-doc §6 024C gated on both halves + FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001\\\": \\\"PASS — §6 024B row + split note confirm 024C gates on both 024B-core + 024B-extras; FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 listed open in STATUS.md.\\\",\\n    \\\"STATUS.md chain entry 2026-05-10\\\": \\\"PASS — 4-row chain entry present covering restore, workflow, break-glass/D-047, and step-7 placeholder/parking-branch note.\\\",\\n    \\\"Anti-descoping\\\": \\\"PASS — step-7 demo is the only merge-blocking AC still open; all other deliverables shipped; no silent drops.\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"invariant_map\\\": {\\n    \\\"Invariant 7 (rollback <30 min SLO)\\\": \\\"ASPIRATIONAL — --restore mode delivered; SLO confirmed only after step-7 real-repo demo (TF-024B-STEP7-DEMO-001, merge-blocking AC unchecked).\\\",\\n    \\\"Invariant 2 (CI-enforced component)\\\": \\\"PASS — .github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml closes the CI-enforcement gap left open after 024B-core shipped the CLI.\\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n```\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"b28301d5-1228-4975-a01b-a993ad6cb082\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.9479084000000002,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":31,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":138516,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":2852508,\"output_tokens\":38045,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":138516,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":1,\"output_tokens\":14696,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":144343,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1554,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":1554},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":1823,\"outputTokens\":26,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.0019529999999999999,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-sonnet-4-6\":{\"inputTokens\":31,\"outputTokens\":38045,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":2852508,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":138516,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":1.9459554000000003,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"4ee28d93-7ef9-455d-95b6-06efb7aacb79\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
