ion-issue` job in `.github/workflows/release-gate.yml` per slice 020H.3.1. The release-gate evaluation job remains `contents: read` only; the new job fires solely on `needs.release-gate.result == 'failure' && github.event_name == 'push'`. Symmetric with D-029 (020C.1 `statuses: write` for readback). Closes WP-SCP-022 020H.3.1 R1 SAFE-MIN-003 + SAFE-MAJ-001.\n- **D-038 (2026-05-02)** — Adopt hash-pinned Python supply-chain installs across the SCP federation primitive's two YAML/JSON-validating workflows per slice 020M (`requirements/policy-check.{in,txt}`; `pip install --require-hashes`). PATCH bump v1.0.0 → v1.0.1. Closes TF-020H3rg-002.\n- **D-039 (2026-05-02)** — Extend the slice 020M hash-pinned Python supply-chain install pattern to the SCP-self conflict-gate workflow per slice 020N (`requirements/conflict-gate.{in,txt}`; `pip install --require-hashes` + `--no-deps` ct-auth + `--no-deps -e .`). No semver bump (conflict-gate.yml is internal-only per VERSIONING.md §\"Scope\"). Closes TF-020M-001.\n- **D-040 (2026-05-02)** — Amend rule-RFC process so 48h is a CEILING (auto-defer trigger) not a FLOOR (minimum wait time) **in single-operator mode** (D-031 default at v1.0.0). Operator may merge as soon as adversarial-review fixpoint reached AND PR is open with `scp-rule-proposal` label. The non-waivable 48h MINIMUM for bypass-introducing proposals (020H.1 R1 SAFE-MAJ-001) is preserved. When 2nd maintainer onboards (D-031 escalation), 48h becomes mandatory MINIMUM. Surfaced by 020L dogfood when operator review of merge-readiness identified the wall-clock pause as theatre rather than safety in single-operator mode (no second pair of eyes for the pause to enable). Symmetric with D-033's \"operational reality must amend the spec\" pattern.\n- **D-041 (2026-05-03)** — Adopt the cross-repo scorecard data shape (`schemas/scorecard-emit.schema.json` v0.1) + opt-in adopter participation model per WP-SCP-023 023B. MAJOR-pinned schema; default-false `scorecard-emit: bool` workflow_call input; OIDC artifact attestation via `actions/attest-build-provenance@v4.1.0`; aggregator verifies at slice 023C via `gh attestation verify --signer-workflow`. NEVER carries waiver content (invariant 2 enforced by schema's `additionalProperties: false`). v1.1.0 → v1.2.0 (MINOR per VERSIONING.md additive-opt-in). Closes plan-doc §9 D-041 reservation.\n- **D-042 (2026-05-03)** — Adopt the cross-repo scorecard aggregator pipeline trust model per WP-SCP-023 023C. Per-emit verification via `gh attestation verify --signer-workflow <expected_workflow_ref>` (mandatory `job_workflow_ref` constraint pre-committed at 023A R2 MAJ-SAFE-R2-001 closure); index trust rooted in git's required-signed-commits + CODEOWNERS + branch protection (NOT a separate Ed25519 layer; Sigstore/Fulcio uses Ed25519 under the hood, managed by GitHub). Two-job permission split (aggregate read-only + commit write-scoped) mirrors 023B's `attest-scorecard` job pattern. Internal-only; no semver bump. Closes plan-doc §9 D-042 reservation.\n- **D-043 (2026-05-03)** — Adopt the cross-repo scorecard exposure surface — markdown report + MCP method `scp.consult_scorecard` — per WP-SCP-023 023D. Markdown generator at `scripts/generate-scorecard-report.py` (deterministic golden-file-tested). MCP method has read-only contract per plan-doc invariant 5 (request: `repo_filter?` + `since_emitted_at?`; response: aggregated counts only, never waiver content per invariant 2; Pydantic-enforced field whitelist). ADOPT-001 §12.7.15 documents the adopter onboarding workflow. Closes plan-doc §9 D-043 reservation.\n\n## Post-Threshold-A backlog\n\n> **Naming note (per 020H.3 + 020H.3.1 disambiguation):** \"020H **part** 3\" (no dot, with the word \"part\") is the pre-Threshold-A v1.0.0-cut sequence slice that landed at PR #75 / commit `347fde2` (ADOPT-001 §12 federation appendix). \"020H**.**3\" (with dot) is the post-Threshold-A dot-N follow-up that landed at PR #79 / commit `42f49db` (release-gate workflow). \"020H**